content.text:
Now action handlers. Insert near top after home. Let's add yt handlers. Need careful targeted updates.

```
if(name.startsWith('yt-')){ ... }
```
But action names include `yt-play`, `yt-select`, `yt-like`, `yt-save`, `yt-sub`, `yt-open`, `yt-tag`, `yt-search-web`. Handle.

Note: `button` may be undefined for some; only use when relevant.

```
if(name==='yt-play'){state.yt.playing=true;complete('video');renderHomes();return}
if(name==='yt-select'){state.yt.current=Number(button.dataset.video);state.yt.playing=true;complete('video');renderHomes();return}
if(name==='yt-tag'){state.yt.tag=button.dataset.tag;renderHomes();return}
if(name==='yt-like'){state.yt.liked=!state.yt.liked;button.classList.toggle('active',state.yt.liked);button.textContent=state.yt.liked?'♥ Liked':'♡ Like';if(state.yt.liked)complete('like');return}
if(name==='yt-save'){...}
if(name==='yt-sub'){...}
if(name==='yt-open'){openExternal(`https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=${ytVideos[state.yt.current].id}`);return}
if(name==='yt-search-web'){openExternal(`https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=${encodeURIComponent(state.yt.query||'trending')}`);return}
```

For `yt-sub`, the button's class `yt-sub` and text. `button.classList.toggle('subbed',...)`. Good.
For `yt-save`, button has class yt-chip; toggle active.
For like similar.

When complete() triggers a toast and quest step; fine. If all done, celebrate. Good.

For save if unsaving no complete. Good.

Potential issue: complete() is called while the button is in current DOM; it doesn't re-render homes. Fine.

Add after `if(name==='home')...`.

